<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>X3Code.Utilities</PackageId>
    <Product>X3Code.Utilities</Product>
    <Title>X3-Code Utilities</Title>
    <Description>Some little helpers for every project</Description>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>10.0.0: New version scheme - the major now tracks the .NET generation the package is built for (net10.0), the minor carries features and breaking changes, the patch carries fixes. All X3Code packages move to 10.0.0 together.
The package now ships its XML documentation, so consumers get IntelliSense. Added an MIT license expression, a README and a symbol package (snupkg) with SourceLink.
Fixed six malformed documentation links that used cref for external URLs instead of href (ArbitraryNumberConverter, RegexUtilities, MimeTypeConverter).
Microsoft.Data.SqlClient 6.1.4 -> 6.1.6.
All asynchronous methods on IBasicHttpClient/BasicHttpClient now take a CancellationToken. The parameter is optional, so existing call sites keep compiling.
Fixed: the generic GetAsync overload started a ReadAsStringAsync task that was never awaited and read the content stream in parallel with the deserialization.
Fixed: UploadStreamAsync never disposed its StreamContent.
BREAKING: DatabaseConnector moved out into its own package, X3Code.Sql.Utils, and into the X3Code.Sql.Utils namespace. It was the only type here that needed Microsoft.Data.SqlClient and pulled that whole graph - Azure.Identity, Microsoft.IdentityModel.*, the native SNI assets - into every consumer of this package. X3Code.Utilities now has no package dependencies at all.
DataRowExtension no longer casts the cell to string. Against a typed DataTable - which is what a database hands back - that threw an InvalidCastException, and it took ToInteger, ToDecimal, ToFloat, ToDouble, ToDateTime, ToBoolean and ToChar down with it. Typed columns are now read natively, so ToDateTime no longer needs a matching pattern for a real date column.
ToChar returns the documented '\0' for an empty column instead of throwing, and signals a too-long value with ArgumentException instead of a bare Exception.
EntityPropertyExtension formats with InvariantCulture. Previously a decimal came out as "42,42" on a machine with a German locale and as "42.42" elsewhere.</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>


</Project>
